# Backend Express Rules

Backend is modular Express.

Rules:
- Controllers stay thin.
- Services contain business logic.
- Validate request bodies with Zod.
- Use centralized error middleware.
- Use auth middleware for protected routes.
- Use role middleware for role-protected routes.
- Use Prisma for database access.
- Use raw SQL only for PostGIS queries if needed.
- Return consistent API responses:
  { success, message, data }
- Never store raw passwords or raw tokens.
- Hash passwords.
- Store only token hashes for invitations and password reset.

When backend API behavior changes:
- Update docs/backend/api-catalog.md
- Update docs/features/<feature>.md
- Update docs/flows/<flow>.md if the user journey changed